37eb591ca8c605696d8c0b33", "parent": "17dca4a1bfefa7b8593be71d49775a3f259e3f5a"}], "patch": "patches/71624c3e49a8eb7b37eb591ca8c605696d8c0b33-1/20260924T153821Z-d1b8fdc9.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "71624c3e49a8eb7b37eb591ca8c605696d8c0b33", "paths": ["lexical-parse-integer/src/shared.rs"]}], "tests": ["i8_decimal_test"]}, "shard": "lexical-core", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix return of negative integers with partial parser.", "summary": "When partial integer parsing encounters an invalid digit after a negative number, it returns the unsigned magnitude without applying the negative sign: parsing \"-1a\" as i8 returns Ok((1, 2)) instead of Ok((-1, 2)). The fix applies wrapping negation before converting the accumulated value to the signed result. The fix adds a detecting assertion to i8_decimal_test in lexical-parse-integer/tests/api_tests.rs. Both reversal regions occur exactly once, and replacing the fixed region restores the parent implementation file exactly. Tests were not run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T15:40:00.316756+00:00"}
