"}], "patch": "patches/0c9456acf484691ef250998fec8ca823241c563c-1/20260924T153940Z-b9047dd0.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "0c9456acf484691ef250998fec8ca823241c563c", "paths": ["lexical-util/src/skip.rs"]}], "tests": ["f64_exponent_internal_digit_separator_test"]}, "shard": "lexical-core", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fixes the `is_contiguous` check on digits iterators.", "summary": "Digit iterators incorrectly delegated bulk reads using the underlying Bytes contiguity flag. A format permitting exponent separators makes Bytes noncontiguous even when its integer iterator is contiguous, causing a debug assertion during parsing of \"31.01e7_1\". The fix passes the digit iterator's own contiguity flag. Reverse only that bulk-read delegation. The existing test is a top-level function in lexical-parse-float/tests/api_tests.rs; select package lexical-parse-float, test target api_tests, with format enabled, compact disabled, and debug assertions enabled. No tests were added by this fix. This plan has not been executed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T15:45:09.685093+00:00"}
